Open source - Using for free without license
   The term open source for first coined by Richard Stallman(RS)
Personalities and their own websites
    Richard Stallman- stallman.org
    Bill Gates-Gates Notes

  While RS working in the UNIX team
  He faced a need for changing the page size of the print xerox sheet.
  So he decides to code the xerox machine by his own.
  While he asked for the dumped code in printing machine his collegous said that we bought the machine
but they did not give the code that is coded in the machine.
  So he admitted that the source code should be open source because we have the right to know the things
in our own products.
  So at that time he coined the term open source
  So after that he quit UNIX and start a canvas for the open source contribution. 
  That is every product that we use, we should able to see the source code in it.
  So, the product's code which was visible to the its users that is called open source.

Community driven vs corporate driven:

Community driven :
            Open source, a group of people can contribute it to its development.
            Aligned with community  & user needs
            Eg: Python(community : Python software foundation)
                Ruby(Ruby community)
                Perl(Perl community)
Corporate driven : 
            Not completely open source, modifications and updates are made by a single company who owns it
            Aligned with corporate goals
            Eg: Java(Oracle owns and standards java)
                c#,Typescript->Microsoft
                Golang,Dart->Google
                R-> R Foundation Heavily supported by microsoft 
                Swift(Apple)
                

Partially open source - some parts of the code or project is open source, others are proprietary
